0..71 Comment "/// This source states the winding number of a loop by transport in the"
72..149 Comment "/// helix over the circle. It follows cctt\'s `tests/bench/s1.cctt`, the first"
150..210 Comment "/// rung of the Brunerie ladder, and the HoTT book\'s § 8.1."
211..214 Comment "///"
215..293 Comment "/// The successor of the presented integers is an equivalence, since its rules"
294..371 Comment "/// cancel a successor with a predecessor. So `ua` makes it a path from `Int`"
372..449 Comment "/// to itself. The helix is `Int` at the point, and that path along the loop."
450..523 Comment "/// The winding number of a loop is the transport of zero along it in the"
524..534 Comment "/// helix."
535..538 Comment "///"
539..617 Comment "/// The checker computes the transport along the empty word. A transport along"
618..652 Comment "/// the loop does not compute yet."
653..656 Comment "///"
657..673 Comment "/// - see: #6268"
674..732 Comment "// The circle, the presented integers and their successor."
